#### Correlation Between Multiplicity in PMD and Other Detectors

After removing bad Runs, scatter plots between \(N_{\gamma-like}\) multiplicity in PMD [72] and charged particle multiplicity in TPC [69] in Au+Au collisions are shown in Figure 3.15. The three panels show the figure for the three different energies, 39, 27 and 19.6 A GeV. A single correlation band is observed between both multiplicities. The correlation band is almost linear for 39 A GeV but shows a clear \(bending\) for 27 A GeV. For 19.6 A GeV the \(bend\) is much more pronounced.

The bending in these plots can be qualitatively understood by realising that with decreasing collision energy, the beam rapidity decreases and gets closer to the acceptance range of PMD. Possible differences between the particle production at mid rapidity and forward rapidity may lead to other phenomena that may give an extra yield on the PMD even for peripheral collisions. Such extra yield may result in a large increase in the multiplicity of the \(bending\).

